
## Array Creation

```text
np.array()             → creates a NumPy array
np.asarray()           → converts input into a NumPy array
np.zeros()             → creates an array filled with 0
np.ones()              → creates an array filled with 1
np.full()              → creates an array filled with a specified value
np.empty()             → creates an uninitialized array
np.zeros_like()        → creates zeros with the same shape as another array
np.ones_like()         → creates ones with the same shape as another array
np.full_like()         → creates an array with the same shape as another array
np.empty_like()        → creates an uninitialized array with the same shape
np.eye()               → creates an identity matrix
np.identity()          → creates an identity matrix
np.arange()            → creates evenly spaced values using a step
np.linspace()          → creates evenly spaced values between two limits
np.logspace()          → creates logarithmically spaced values
np.geomspace()         → creates geometrically spaced values
np.meshgrid()          → creates coordinate grids
np.diag()              → creates/extracts a diagonal
np.diagflat()          → creates a diagonal matrix from flattened input
np.tri()               → creates a triangular matrix
np.vander()            → creates a Vandermonde matrix
np.fromiter()          → creates an array from an iterable
np.fromstring()        → creates an array from a string
np.frombuffer()        → creates an array from a buffer
```

