# Searching / Finding

```text
np.argmax()             → index of the largest value
np.argmin()             → index of the smallest value
np.nanargmax()          → index of largest non-NaN value
np.nanargmin()          → index of smallest non-NaN value
np.where()              → finds indices based on a condition
np.nonzero()            → finds indices of non-zero elements
np.argwhere()           → returns indices where condition is true
np.flatnonzero()        → returns flattened indices of non-zero elements
np.searchsorted()       → finds where values should be inserted
```

For example:

```python
a = np.array([10, 20, 30, 40])

np.argmax(a)
```

```text
3
```

Because `40` is at index `3`.

